#X obj 250 1918 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 1918 onsets;
#X text 270 1918 analyzes the source array for onsets using the aubio
library. Available detection methods: 'default' — aubio's default (currently
equivalent to 'hfc') \, 'hfc' — High Frequency Content: emphasizes
energy in the high-frequency range \, works well for percussive onsets
\, 'energy' — Energy: detects onsets by local changes in the overall
signal energy \, 'complex' — Complex Domain: compares the predicted
and actual spectral content \, good for tonal and complex sounds \,
'phase' — Phase Deviation: detects sudden changes in the phase of the
signal \, 'wphase' — Weighted Phase Deviation: like 'phase' \, but
weighting phase changes by magnitude \, 'specdiff' — Spectral Difference:
measures the difference between consecutive spectra \, 'kl' — Kullback–Liebler
divergence of successive spectra \, 'mkl' — Modified Kullback–Liebler
divergence \, 'specflux' — Spectral Flux: sums positive changes in
the magnitude spectrum \, classic onset detection function. Arguments
are:;
#X obj 300 2200 cnv 1 124 21 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 300 2200 [METHOD=default]: onset detection method. Type: symbol.
Allowed values: default \, hfc \, energy \, complex \, phase \, wphase
\, specdiff \, kl \, mkl \, specflux.;
